{"content":[{"c":["HELKATH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["First of 22 cities mentioned in the territory allotted to Asher’s tribe for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.25","r":"Josh.19.25","rawR":"Josh.19.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.25","value":"Josh.19.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:25"},"). Helkath was one of four cities in Asher given to the Levitical Gershonite families (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.31","r":"Josh.21.31","rawR":"Josh.21.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.31","value":"Josh.21.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"21:31"},"). It is alternately spelled Hukok in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.75","r":"1Chr.6.75","rawR":"1Chr.6.75","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.75","value":"1Chr.6.75"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:75"},". Its ancient site is perhaps located at the modern Tell el-Harbaj."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Helkath","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 19:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.25","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.25","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.25"},{"anchorText":"21:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.31","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.31","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.31"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 6:75","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.75","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.75","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.75"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7d9f3a753f942d00b12ad29ae7f2346d8581358c33f1352462b4e92ab20b7334","sourceItemName":"Helkath","sourceItemOrder":231,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Helkath","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Helkath","title":"Helkath","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}